    "text": "Borvo was the Gaulish god of the healing springs. He is also called Bormanus and Bormo. He is the male form of the goddess Ulkin. The plural form is the Suleviae. Artists drew him as a warrior. A horned serpent rested beneath him. He was the son of the goddess Sirona. He was the consort of Damona, dubbed Bormana. The Romans held he was the same as Apollo. His name may mean to boil. That fits a god of the hot springs.",
